**The cutoff changed.** The objective now excludes only work first published after
**2026-10-18** (the delivered study used 2026-09-01). `idea-repo` brief v4 Sec. 5: arXiv
2610.02344 (v1 2026-10-01, "Drive vs. Decay: On the Training Dynamics of JEPAs") linearises the
JEPA flow at the trivial point, defines a per-mode stability ratio mu_i = gamma_i/sigma_i whose
count of unstable modes tracks reachable rank, unifies predictor scaling, masking and EMA as
shifts of mu, and proposes ResidualPred (identity-biased transformer predictor) that raises rank
in I-JEPA (CIFAR-10/100, STL-10, ImageNet); public code at commit 3176215b (2026-10-01); arXiv
comment: accepted at NeurIPS 2026, 10 pages main text. The
delivered paper's framing alone is therefore no longer novel; what may remain distinct (race and
capture with a stable collapsed point, lambda^race, predictor-decay necessity, pre-registered
held-out tests) and what the extension adds must be shown against it. Also relevant:
2609.35288 (lambda-JEPA, layer balance in two-layer linear JEPAs; deep encoders, rung C1).

